  "reason": "The records collectively make the proposal plausible. R3 directly establishes combined high-pressure/high-temperature processing in a closely related HEA, while the other high-pressure studies show that pressure can overcome kinetic barriers and reorganize HEA structures through stacking faults, dislocations, and twinning. R2, R10, and R16 establish the FCC/B2 lamellar starting structure and the mechanical cooperation of soft FCC and hard B2 phases in the Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni eutectic system. R4 further shows coherent nanoscale structures in nearly the same alloy composition, and R5-R8/R18 identify stacking faults, twins, dislocations, and transformations as synergistic ductility mechanisms. No single record demonstrates HPHT-induced hierarchical coherent FCC/B2 interfaces or preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer, but an expert could plausibly combine these teachings to propose HPHT as a route to interface reconstruction and multimode deformation in this alloy."
